Having been a huge fan of FarCry 2, I was looking forward to more hardcore, do-or-die gunplay out in the wilderness. FarCry 3 proves to be worse than FC2 in many ways, which I will list below:
@Perma-HUD - You always have a map and your objectives on-screen, removing immersion. FC2 was cinematic.
@Low-quality audio - Just check the forums. Almost all the audio sounds like it's being played back from a 50's radio. The audio for the game is also incredibly low. When I normally play games on 4, this game requires 21 to be heard.
@AC3 Crafting - Did you like crafting player upgrades via random collection items, like in Assassin's Creed 3? No? Well, FC3 will have you hunt down x_number of animal to arbitrarily upgrade some part of your equipment. Better keep your eye out for pigs, or your money will quickly max-out.
@Magic AI - A silenced sniper shot, killing a lone guard behind a wall will still alert the entire camp, and have them lobbing grenades at you, despite not 'detecting' you yet.
@AC Towers - Ubisoft, remaining forever inventive, have introduced Assassins Creed's 'eagle towers' inorder to map out the land. They are equally challenging, with a similar 'press-button-to-win' climbing technique.
@Awful Protagonist/s - If you don't immidiately hate your shitbag character and all his friends from the intro cutscene, something is wrong with you. FC2 gave you a silent protagonist, which you could chose from an array of nationalities. Your frathouse-♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ character also goes from rich ♥♥♥♥♥ to one-man-army in one day. He laos has a magical tattoo that inks itself. If you were hoping for realism, that's going right out the ♥♥♥♥ing window.
@Uplay - Unlike FC2, FC3 requires Uplay and a Ubisoft account, despite being bought through steam. Acheivements are also not on Steam, making them worthless.
@Comparatively Ugly - The graphics of FC2 were mind-blowing when it came out - the Crysis of its time. FC3's graphics are... frankly the same, if not worse. I've got a♥♥♥♥♥♥framerate on medium-high specs, and it feels as much of a plastic videogame as any other - certainly nothing as immersive as FC2. Always-on HUD, glowing interactables, stagger-stepping animal AI... The whole thing is ugly and underwhelming.
Frankly, FC3 is not worth your money or your time. Go get FC2, whack the difficulty to max, and have the most intense shooter experiance of your gamer life.

