Pros:
+ Giant open world filled with foes and animals;
+ A surprisingly engaging main storyline;
+ Tons of things to do apart from the main quests;
+ A solid crafting system;
+ Weapon customization;
+ A well-made stealth system;
+ Superb graphics with a robust soundtrack;
Cons:
- Crashes often (at least for me), stability and graphical issues;
- Outpost difficulty varies from hard to "shoot the cage with the tiger in it and watch it devour 10 dudes";
- The hero is extremely boring from a voice acting perspective, horrible miscast;
- Glitches!
- uPlay.
A huge game with plenty of content to keep you in it.

